- The `if` condition checks if `a` is greater than `b`. If true, it prints "Case1".
- The `elif` (else if) condition checks if `a` is less than `b`. If true, it prints "Case2".
- If neither condition is met (i.e., `a == b`), nothing is printed.

This structure efficiently handles both cases without redundancy.

